## Reviewer points not applied

- Space as the Latvian thousands separator, and currency after the amount, is the native norm. The lv number checker cannot parse it (R14). Amounts stay "TWD 500.000" / "TWD 1.579.589".
- "TWD 1.57M" is pinned. The suggested "1,57 miljonu TWD" was not applied.
- "2025. gada 13. septembrī" is natural Latvian and is what the checker comment documents, but at the start of date_display the checker deletes "2025. " as a list marker. date_display stays "13. septembrī 2025".
- "vienu gadu" / "vienu darba stāža gadu" / "viens mazs kravas automobilis" / "pieckārtīgai" drop a counted digit. Digits were kept inside the corrected phrases.
- Turning Q16–Q20 into headings, and deleting U+200B blanks, would fail headings, blocks, and ZWSP parity with the Korean source.
- Hangul slugs in url were not edited.
- "gan galīgo reklāmu" is accusative. After "jāpārskata" the nominative "galīgā reklāma" is the form that agrees.
- Merging the 013/015 comma fragment with the next block would change the block count. Each block was completed on its own.
- "gaita" was not replaced everywhere. It is the right word for a course of events, and the reviewer's 016 rewrite still says "Kuras valsts gaita".
- Statutory ceilings ("visaugstāk 6 mēnešu alga", the 5 % undistributed-earnings surcharge) are legal ceilings, not advertising superlatives. Left.
- 003 "brīdinājuma zīmes" is a warning sign, not the resignation-notice calque. Left.
